  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The Bounce – wall pass in the middle and a finish off the corner pass",
  "description": "Half court, one goal with a goalkeeper. Two lines at the centre line, one by each board, with the balls in the right line. C stands in the left corner. B, first in the right line, carries the ball diagonally in towards the middle and passes to A in the left line, who plays it straight back. B then passes to C in the corner and moves in towards goal on the left side. C passes in and B shoots first time.\n\nRotation: the shooter stays in the corner, C goes to the left line and A to the right line. Switch sides after a few minutes.\n\nVariant: C chooses between passing in to B and shooting themselves, so B has to be ready for both. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The wall pass should be firm and put in front of B, so the speed is kept."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "B: move towards goal straight after the pass to the corner."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Time the run so you arrive as C passes."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Shoot first time in front of goal."
    }
  ],
